@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# P0 pure-Cube companion
+
+These new modules and the accompanying `tests/test_cosim_*.py` files were
+created for the TileLang Ascend 950 distributed P0 implementation on
+2026-10-23. They are distributed from TileLang's `tools/cannsim/` bundle;
+`cosim/LICENSE` preserves the TileLang repository license for these additions.
+They are not an upstream cannsim-helper release.
+
+The compatibility base is cannsim-helper commit
+`2eb1ce5a79a76cc3f3e1c0eb4b04c6e9f6f694cf` from
+`https://gitcode.com/Withinlover/cannsim-helper`.
+The pinned tree has no license file. This companion does not grant or infer a
+license for that existing upstream tree and does not modify its tracked files.
+
+`protocol.py`, `worker.py`, and the original segment/protocol/worker tests come
+from the locally developed dual-rank extension. `segments.py` uses the new
+`runtime.py` to adapt to the base revision's two-argument `record_environment`
+API. This adapter accepts only explicit scheduler-fix mode `off`; no MIX
+scheduler repair, Flash Attention changes, or precompiled object is included.
+The helper's original mixed-core default is retained. P0 explicitly selects
+`expected_cores=("AIC",)` for its pure-Cube object.
+
+This is a CPU communication protocol model combined with independent
+single-device CANN recordings. It does not execute real inter-device transfers
+or certify multi-device performance.
